IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Newfoundland and Labrador Income and Employment Support Act and Regulations -- the time limits that bind the
-- applicant or recipient, and what the department and the appeal board must then do for them. Kept apart from
-- nl-ies.l4 because it needs dates (daydate).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Time limits for the applicant or recipient`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the recipient`
    `the internal reviewer`
    `the appeal board`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `provide the information requested`
    `request an internal review in writing`
    `perform the internal review`
    `appeal in writing to the appeal board`
    `hear the appeal`

§§ `Reg s 5(2) and (5) -- answering a written request for information`

-- Reg s 5(2): "an officer may require, in writing, that the recipient provide additional information to assess the
-- recipient's eligibility and the recipient shall comply in a manner acceptable to the minister within 30 days of the
-- request being made by the officer." s 5(3): the officer may make exceptions to that time. s 5(5): where the recipient
-- fails to comply in time, "the officer may deny, vary, suspend or cancel that recipient's income support". The days
-- are counted from the request; an exception granted by the officer is an input (extra days).
GIVEN `extra days allowed by the officer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to answer the request for information` `extra days allowed by the officer` MEANS
    PARTY `the recipient`
    MUST  `provide the information requested`
    WITHIN 30 PLUS `extra days allowed by the officer`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the recipient` BECAUSE "information not provided within 30 days of the officer's written request: the officer may deny, vary, suspend or cancel income support (reg s 5(5))"

GIVEN `the date of the request` IS A DATE, `extra days allowed by the officer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to answer` MEANS `the date of the request` PLUS 30 PLUS `extra days allowed by the officer`

§§ `Act s 41 -- internal review`

-- Act s 41(2), (3): an applicant or recipient "may request an internal review" of a decision on income support, on
-- employment support, or of an underpayment or overpayment; the request "shall be made in writing ... no later than 60
-- days after being notified". s 41(5): "An internal review shall be performed within 15 days of the receipt of the
-- written request for it". The days run from the notice of the decision; once the request is made, the 15 days of the
-- review start.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my right to an internal review` MEANS
    PARTY `the recipient`
    MAY   `request an internal review in writing`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE (PARTY `the internal reviewer`
           MUST  `perform the internal review`
           WITHIN 15
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST  BREACH BY `the internal reviewer` BECAUSE "internal review not performed within 15 days of receipt of the written request (Act s 41(5))")

GIVEN `the date I was notified of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to request an internal review` MEANS `the date I was notified of the decision` PLUS 60

§§ `Act s 43 -- appeal to the appeal board`

-- Act s 43(2): "An appeal under this section shall be made in writing no more than 60 days from the receipt of the
-- outcome of an internal review". s 41(5): the person "is considered to have received the outcome of the internal review
-- 7 business days after it has been decided" (the receipt date is asked as a fact, since business days depend on the
-- holiday calendar). s 43(3)(e): the board shall "within 30 days of receiving the appeal, hear the appeal".
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my right to appeal` MEANS
    PARTY `the recipient`
    MAY   `appeal in writing to the appeal board`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE (PARTY `the appeal board`
           MUST  `hear the appeal`
           WITHIN 30
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST  BREACH BY `the appeal board` BECAUSE "appeal not heard within 30 days of its receipt (Act s 43(3)(e))")

GIVEN `the date I received the outcome of the internal review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to appeal` MEANS `the date I received the outcome of the internal review` PLUS 60
